{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Linear System.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Linear System.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"linear system linear system","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Linear System.md","fileName":"Linear System.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Linear System","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 19:44\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Linear System Structure]] · [[Matrix Algebra for Statistical Models]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Linear System Structure","Matrix Algebra for Statistical Models","Coefficient Matrix","appliedlinearalgebraandoptimizationusingmatlab.pdf","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Linear System.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Linear System.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"linear system linear system","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Linear System.md","fileName":"Linear System.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Linear System","heading":"Linear System","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A linear system is a collection of linear equations in common unknowns. It can be written compactly as $Ax=b$, using a [[Coefficient Matrix]] $A$, an unknown vector $x$, and a right-hand-side vector $b$.\n\nDepending on rank and dimensions, a system may have one solution, no solution, or infinitely many solutions. Numerical methods exploit matrix structure to solve it efficiently and accurately.\n\nThe source introduces matrix algebra through simultaneous scalar equations and then returns to the same structure when solving least-squares normal equations. Whether the coefficient matrix has independent columns determines whether the fitted parameter vector is uniquely identifiable.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Linear System Structure","Matrix Algebra for Statistical Models","